<title>GERMANY: Douglas first half sales up 2.2 pct.</title>
<headline>Douglas first half sales up 2.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HAGEN, Germany 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30.</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group sales			    1,890	vs  1,850</p>
<p>    Of which: foreign sales		284	vs    245</p>
<p>    Investments				 64	vs     47</p>
<p>    Depreciation				68	vs     64</p>
<p>    Number of workers		   13,600	vs 13,517</p>
<p>    Of which: abroad		     2,129	vs  1,915</p>
<p>    Number of branches		   1,801	vs  1,811</p>
<p>    Of which: abroad			 282	vs    262</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German perfumery store group is Douglas Holding AG. The company said that first half group operating profits were &quot;somewhat below&quot; a year earlier due to a high advertising spend.</p>
<p>First half same-store sales grew by 0.8 percent.</p>
<p>Douglas also forecast group sales of 4.5 billion marks this year and said it was optimistic of achieving a &quot;good&quot; earnings result this year. Sales last year were 4.3 billion marks, and group net profits rose 2.1 percent to 105.6 million marks.</p>
</text>
